  "reply_raw": "The ten cases admitted share one shape: urgent wires on acct-vendor, any amount, internal or partner counterparty, dual signature on file. That is a coherent class, and a rule with no lower bound on amount would authorize arbitrary future amounts unattended. Since no case here was denied or capped, the evidence supports the class itself but not unlimited size, so I'll propose a standing rule that keeps a ceiling in place rather than opening the resource entirely.\n\n{\"mode\": \"precedent\", \"rule\": {\"action\": \"wire_transfer\", \"resource\": \"acct-vendor\", \"conditions\": {\"urgency\": [\"eq\", \"1\"], \"amount_usd\": [\"le\", \"100000\"], \"dual_sign\": [\"eq\", \"1\"]}}}",
